+/*
+ * Stalled mutant waits. Spider-Man's Bink pairs its decode thread with the
+ * game thread through two mutants, and once in a while (after many movies)
+ * a hand-off between them goes missing: each thread waits forever on a
+ * mutant the other holds and the movie stops on a black frame. Mutants are
+ * host mutexes here; which hand-off is lost is not known.
+ *
+ * The title's frame watchdog (xbox_BreakStalledWaits) calls when nothing has
+ * been presented for a few seconds. An INFINITE wait that includes a mutant
+ * is waited in slices, and gives up with STATUS_TIMEOUT once such a call
+ * comes in after it started: Bink takes that as not getting the lock, goes
+ * on, and the deadlock comes apart. No other wait is touched.
